- op: discuss  # d196
  at: '2026-10-11T05:50:31Z'  # d196
  by: agent  # d196
  actor: jgstern_agent  # d196
  clock: 3  # d196
  nonce: d196  # d196
  message: "Fixed in PR #1529 (merge 70ca0396e5). Root cause: main's --backend pre-scan looped range(len(argv) - 1), so the last token was never examined, even in the self-contained '=' form. Same loop also bypassed argparse's choices= (the flag is stripped before argparse runs), so an unknown value like '--backend bogus' was silently ignored and the command ran. Fix: new _strip_backend_flag(argv, parser) scans every token (stopping at '--'), reads the value token only when it exists and is not another option, and rejects a missing value ('expected one argument') or unknown one ('invalid choice') via parser.error, exit 2; choices come from one BACKEND_CHOICES tuple shared with add_argument. Evidence on dev 70ca0396e5: 'hypergumbo catalog --backend=tree-sitter' -> exit 0, prints the catalog ('Suggested for current repo: ...'); 'hypergumbo catalog --backend' -> exit 2 'argument --backend: expected one argument'; 'hypergumbo catalog --backend=bogus' -> exit 2 'argument --backend: invalid choice: 'bogus' (choose from tree-sitter, rust-analyzer, scip-python)'. Tests: test_backend_cli_flag.py (=-form last, =-form sole token, trailing bare --backend, --backend followed by a flag, unknown choice in 5 positions, -- terminator). Analogues: no other pre-scanned flag in main has a lookahead (--debug and --help/--all are membership tests)."  # d196
